I am using Hibernate 6.6 with Envers and hypersistence-utils-hibernate-63. I have a JSON column defined as follows: 
 @Type(JsonStringType.class)
@Column(name = "MYPROP", length = 4000)
private List<MyType> myTypes = new ArrayList<>();

 The MyType class uses a custom JSON deserializer to handle a legacy representation of the data: 
 @JsonDeserialize(using = MyTypeDeserializer.class)
public class MyType implements Serializable {
 // implementation details
}

 This setup works perfectly for standard Hibernate CRUD operations. However, when I fetch an Envers revision using: 
 myTypeRepository.findRevisions(oid)

 The entity returned by revision.getEntity() does not seem to use MyTypeDeserializer . Instead of a list of MyType objects, the myTypes property contains a list of LinkedHashMap objects. 
 Is there a way to configure Hibernate Envers to respect the Jackson @JsonDeserialize annotation or force it to use the custom deserializer?

